    {
      "text": "Joseph Smith … the first elder of this church, D&C 20:2. elders of the church … bear witness to the words, D&C 20:16. An apostle is an elder, D&C 20:38. Every elder … is to be ordained according to the gifts, D&C 20:60. elders … to meet in conference once in three months, D&C 20:61 (20:81). children … bring them unto the elders … bless them, D&C 20:70. elders, priests and teachers of this church shall teach, D&C 42:12. elders of the church, two or more, shall be called, D&C 42:44. elders … to conduct all meetings … by the Holy Spirit, D&C 46:2. elders … shall render an account of their stewardship, D&C 72:5. high priests should travel, and also the elders, D&C 84:111 (124:137). until mine elders are endowed with power, D&C 105:11. first elders … should receive their endowment, D&C 105:33. office of an elder comes under the priesthood, D&C 107:7. high priest and elder are to administer, D&C 107:12. must needs be presiding elders, D&C 107:60. duty of the president over the office of elders, D&C 107:89. Send forth the elders of my church unto the nations, D&C 133:8. faithful elders … preaching … in the great world of the spirits, D&C 138:57.",
